      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "second life did something like this and sadly it severely hurt the platform to a point of no return.. people would join the platform to scam users out of money or even copy content to then sell it for less...\nNot just that it drastically changed what uploaded worlds turned out to be.. most of the worlds became market places or glorified stores (although to have a world also costed money as users were responsible for paying server costs which were really steep). \nI foresee many problems too with a currency.. legal issues.. gambling concerns is only a small one of those.. but also since once you have a currency you can exchange back and forth you essentially become a sort of bank.. Things go downhill from there.\nSadly now most of second life revolves just around money and I fear the same would happen to vrchat.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
