  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So firstly this is just my opinion and personally, i believe it would be alot better way of monetizing vrchat than vrchat plus  but i already know alot of people will already hate this idea\ni think vrchat should have a currency system that you buy for real money and you should be able to withdraw this currency out of the game and convert them to real money again whit a fixed exchange rate \nthis should give avatar creators the ability to monetize their avatars so on\nthe way i think it should work is simply that an avatar pillar would have a price if its a monetized avatar when you click on it it would somehow preview the avatar and let you see emotes features and so on instead of just instant just buying and changing whit a click you would have to confirm you want to buy it \navatar creators would have to get certified before being able to use this feature (to prevent junk spam overpriced avatars) \nthere is alot of other stuff that would have to go through for this to work and i can even see alot of ways for this to work in tantrum whit vrchat plus example maby a lover exchange rate if you have it?  or something else like that \nthe way vrchat would make money from this is obviously by charging more for the currency than what they payout \non a sidenote about vrchat plus even tho, i disagree whit the way its done im still gonna buy it simply to support a game i love and i personally think the new nameplates look sick though i hope there will be a way to keep the old and colors on them",
